{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-written miniature of a factory diagnostic database JSON export,",
    "shaped exactly like a real one but small enough to review by eye.",
    "It exists so the golden tests/uds/fixtures/mini.dcat can be recompiled in",
    "CI without the 6.8 MB factory export. Coverage on purpose: a merged",
    "two-service group, a duplicated field qualifier (within one group AND",
    "across groups), signed scaling, an enum with a sentinel row, ASCII and",
    "HEXDUMP fields, an internal presentation, a non-SAFE_READ routine, and a",
    "group needing session (client level 5) and security (level 3).",
    "Also, for the §5.1a/§5.1b naming and array rules: group 0x0101 needs rule",
    "(b) (two services, one presentation name); 0x0208 is a 4-element",
    "collapsible array; 0xF1AA needs rule (c), because ONE service contributes",
    "two identically named fields and no factory name separates them — the",
    "only rule-(c) case anywhere, since the real BMS never produces one.",
    "0x0102 is the trap: THREE same-named presentations at constant stride 16",
    "that must NOT collapse, because their services differ by words, not",
    "numbers — the shape that would fuse a real database's max/min/mean",
    "readings into a bogus array if the collapse guards were dropped.",
    "Compile: script/uds_catalog.py compile tests/uds/fixtures/mini-source.json",
    "         --ecu MINI --variant Mini_Var --all -o tests/uds/fixtures/mini.dcat"
  ],
